design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:6:The thumb control: one rounded rectangular nub in a raised frame, on the joystick side of the band at -78 degrees (78 degrees from the top; the ring has no record button, the joystick is the one control). It tilts; under it five switches (SW1 up, SW3 down, SW4 toward the hand, SW5 toward the fingertip, Alps SKTAAAE010, 2.6 x 1.6 x 0.53 each) sit in a cross at 2.4 mm from the centre, and the centre switch SW2 sits between them (17.15). A press on the centre closes SW2; a long press of 1.0 s starts or stops a recording (17.11). The nub with its flange is one moulded part (architecture 17.3). Before v5: four switches in a cross at 2.1 mm at +150 degrees.
design/mfg/specs/body.md:8:The one-piece metal body of the ring: a flat block (holds screen, board, glass) that flows through two shoulders into an 8.0 mm wide band that goes round the finger. The band is a hollow channel, open toward the finger, later closed by the band liner (specs/band-liner.md). It carries the pockets and openings for the screen, glass, 2 microphone floor pockets with their holes and seats on the underside, 2 floor slots, the joystick opening and pocket, and the motor pocket. The ring has one control, the joystick (17.11): no record button, no record cap and no opening for one. The four charging pads sit in the liner on the inside of the band, so the body has no pad holes (17.12). Before v5 this page listed microphone wall slots, a record cap opening, 4 pad holes and the joystick at 150 degrees.
design/mfg/specs/body.md:78:| motor diameter (pocket is larger) | 5.0 mm, pocket 5.2 mm | ISO 2768-f | Jinlong W0525AB001D, pocket at -44 deg (US 9), joystick-side shoulder; before v5: 7.0 mm at 51 deg |
design/mfg/specs/body.md:90:Floor slots 2.6 x 0.6 at Y = +-5.9, X = -2.2 (two) (corrected 2026-11-11 from X = -4.7: inside model, thin-notes.md K7; assembly.md conflict K-A10; model v5 keeps X -2.2). The slot depth is 1.2 at US 9; the depth per ring size follows from the next model version (17.24 K25: at US 13 each ribbon runs through 0.23 cubic mm of metal between the slot and the band channel). Beside each slot, under the board, 2.6 x 2.2 x 1.03 mm stay free for one ribbon fold (K-A6). The channel ends at 30 degrees. Panel pocket = panel + 0.05 per side (27.45 x 12.9), corner radius 0.1. The microphone pockets, holes and seats are in the table above; no microphone slot exists in any wall. These are the modeller's choices; the maker takes the STEP file for the final geometry once the parts helper has delivered it.
design/mfg/specs/body.md:122:design/architecture.md lines 417, 418, 420, 424, 428-444 (17.1 to 17.3), 469-470 (S12, S13), 488-494 (17.8), 17.10 line 514 on (before v5 it set the motor at 51 deg); 17.11, 17.12, 17.15, 17.19, 17.23 and 17.24 (the newest; they win: joystick at -78 deg, motor 5.0 x 2.5 at -44 deg, microphone floor pockets, no pad holes); 17.7 at lines 478-482 is replaced; design/bom.csv line 53; design/mech/mech-notes.md line 7; design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md.
design/mfg/specs/band-flex-tails.md:9:- FLEX1, joystick side (-Y): carries the vibration motor and the five joystick switches SW1 to SW5, SW2 being the centre switch under the nub (17.11, 17.14). The ring has no record switch and no record button.
design/mfg/specs/band-flex-tails.md:35:| switch pad group count, FLEX1 | 5 | not a dimension | the five joystick switches SW1 to SW5 (SW2 centre) on the same tail; before v5: four switches plus a record switch |
